        "number": 7,
        "title": "Death On-Board",
        "pageRefs": [
          7,
          8
        ],
        "group": "emergency",
        "priority": 10,
        "hasBoatActions": true,
        "synonyms": [
          "death",
          "died",
          "dead",
          "fatality",
          "deceased"
        ],
        "intro": "Should any competitor die during the course of the race:",
        "sections": [
          {
            "actor": "boat",
            "heading": "Rowing Boat Actions (solo entries can ignore this section)",
            "note": "",
            "steps": [
              "Contact Safety Officer via satellite telephone",
              "If unable to contact Safety Officer, contact NMOC via satellite telephone.",
              "If unable to contact Safety Officer or NMOC 7.1.3.1 Issue Mayday message via VHF or any other recognised means available 7.1.3.2 If no response to Mayday, activate your 406MHz EPIRB.",
              "Ensure that all communications equipment is switched on, working and remains switched on.",
              "Ensure AIS is switched on and working and remains switched on.",
              "Deploy the sea anchor to slow the movement of the rowing boat, which will reduce the search area.",
              "The body must be kept on-board the rowing boat and actions taken to preserve the body in the best condition possible",
              "On rendezvous with the Safety Vessel, comply with any enquiry which will include providing a written and signed statement along with any photographs or video to support that statement."
            ]
          },
          {
            "actor": "shore",
            "heading": "Safety Officer Actions",
            "note": "Note: Receipt of an emergency distress message can be either from a rowing boat or NMOC",
            "steps": [
              "On receiving notice of an emergency distress message or EPIRB activation ensure that the following parties are informed immediately: NMOC Atlantic Campaigns SL Management",
              "Contact Safety Vessel(s) and request Safety Vessel assistance",
              "Establish Safety Vessel’s location and ETA at the rowing boat’s last known position.",
              "Establish and maintain an Incident Log",
              "Maintain contact with all the above parties and establish a communications link between the Safety Vessel(s) and Race Headquarters during the enquiry."
            ]
          },
          {
            "actor": "shore",
            "heading": "Safety Vessel Actions",
            "note": "",
            "steps": [
              "Following notification from the Safety Officer, Safety Vessel to proceed directly towards the Rowing Boat",
              "On rendezvous with rowing boat, hold an enquiry at the very first opportunity but at least within 6 hours, and compile a written report which includes: 7.3.2.1 A written and signed statement by the surviving team partner(s) and any other witnesses. 7.3.2.2 Photographs or video to support the written report. Note: It is essential that all parties make a written statement of his/her observations at this time whilst the incident is fresh in everyone’s mind",
              "Wherever possible, the body should be retained for post-mortem examination (please refer to ‘The Ship Captain’s Medical Guide’ for instructions on how to prepare a body for storage or burial at sea)",
              "If it is necessary to bury the body at sea: 7.3.4.1 Photographs and video of the burial should be taken. 7.3.4.2 Record in the official logbook the exact time and place of burial"
            ]
          },
          {
            "actor": "shore",
            "heading": "Atlantic Campaigns SL Management Actions",
            "note": "",
            "steps": [
              "At the earliest opportunity, subject to the facts of the incident being clearly established, a member of Atlantic Campaigns SL Management, accompanied by a police officer will inform the next-of-kin of the people directly involved in person.",
              "If the next-of-kin of the people are overseas, inform them at the earliest opportunity. Consider seeking advice from British Embassy/Consulate",
              "Provide the next-of-kin with a contact phone number for an Atlantic Campaigns SL Incident Liaison Officer (not the Safety Officer)",
              "Liaise with Atlantic Campaigns SL Press Officer to draft a press statement.",
              "All staff to gather for a full briefing on the incident and to take all phone enquiries relating to the incident, providing a prepared and agreed statement and response. The exact response will be determined by Atlantic Campaigns SL Management",
              "Ensure letters are written to next-of-kin – Carsten Heron Olsen CEO to follow up.",
              "Advise insurers."
            ]
          }
        ]
